Luck gains from sacrifices are not fixed at 1 point; it's 0 to +5, 
according to the luck spoiler.

Luck gains and losses are really very well understood, so I would 
suggest a different method:

First, get a blessed luckstone. This is so your luck won't change on its 
own. (it might as well be blessed since you don't want to be unlucky)

Next, max out your luck. Unicorns or sacrificing are easy methods. When 
you're done you know your luck is at 13.

Next, go into Sokoban and lose 5 luck. I suggest Newton's 3rd Law as 
it's very easy/safe to do. Now your luck is at 8.

The favor roll is d(8+6=14)/2 so the highest you can roll is a 7, giving 
you a spellbook. So long as you ALWAYS pray at reconcilliation you're 
safe. With the luckstone your luck is GUARANTEED to stay at 8.


One problem would be if you miss the reconcilliation message (i.e. the 
timeout didn't get zero'd by a sacrifice). If your next sacrifice grants 
you a clover you can't be sure about your luck. In this case I recommend 
maxing again and going down 5 points to be safe.


